**Effect is not BEAM.** Fibers do not provide private process heaps or OTP restart strategies. A durable operation needs storage and a recovery owner.

Use [the durability skill](/skills/durability) to review a design. [The durability system page](/systems/durability) shows the patterns rat-stack ships. These pages separate the book principles from our Effect 4.0.0 mappings.

The template pins Effect 4.0.0. Each named API and each absence claim was checked against that release. Check your own Effect [pin](/skills/gardener) before you apply a mapping.

## Reading order

- [Effect is not BEAM](/lore/effect-is-not-beam): Fibers share a runtime; [scope](/lore/scopes-own-resources) ownership does not supply isolated heaps or OTP restart strategies.
- [Durable work needs storage](/lore/durable-work-needs-storage): A restarted worker cannot recover intent that existed only in memory.
- [Every task needs an owner](/lore/every-task-needs-an-owner): Give child work a lifetime, a failure observer, and a recovery decision.
- [Supervision chooses what restarts](/lore/supervision-is-a-recovery-policy): Restart policy follows dependency shape and bounds repeated recovery.
- [Restart must reconstruct known state](/lore/restart-from-known-state): Execution recovery and state recovery need separate contracts.
- [Retry needs idempotent effects](/lore/retry-needs-idempotency): Repeating an operation must preserve its intended observable result.
- [Checkpoints follow the promised commit](/lore/checkpoints-follow-commits): Persist state and progress together when one store can transact both.
- [Replay needs stable inputs](/lore/replay-needs-stable-inputs): Historical processing must not silently depend on today’s clock or external decisions.
- [Old events must still decode](/lore/old-events-must-still-decode): Retained data needs compatibility rules before recovery depends on it.
- [Dead letters need a return path](/lore/dead-letters-need-a-return-path): Exhausted work needs durable evidence, an owner, and deliberate redrive.
- [Timeouts bound waiting](/lore/timeouts-bound-waiting): A local timeout stops waiting; it does not prove the remote action never happened.
- [Retry load needs a budget](/lore/retry-load-needs-a-budget): One retry owner must control attempts, delay, and aggregate load.
- [Circuit breakers have state](/lore/circuit-breakers-have-state): A breaker stops doomed calls and controls probes before restoring traffic.
- [Bulkheads isolate scarce capacity](/lore/bulkheads-isolate-capacity): Reserve independent capacity for workloads that must not starve each other.
- [Backpressure reaches the producer](/lore/backpressure-reaches-the-producer): Bounded consumption helps only when upstream respects waiting or refusal.
- [Admission control protects recovery](/lore/admission-controls-new-work): Refuse or defer work that cannot be served usefully under current load.
- [Steady state recycles resources](/lore/steady-state-recycles-resources): Every accumulation needs a deliberate recycling policy.
- [Queries need result bounds](/lore/queries-need-result-bounds): Limit result cardinality before the driver materializes an oversized response.
- [Failures keep their meaning](/lore/failures-keep-their-meaning): Expected refusals, infrastructure faults, and defects need different policies.
- [Cleanup can be an idempotent postcondition](/lore/cleanup-can-be-an-idempotent-postcondition): Already-absent state can be success when absence is the operation’s intended result.
- [Pure cores reduce timeline coupling](/lore/pure-cores-reduce-timelines): Move deterministic rules out of time-dependent actions and shared mutable state.
- [Recovery needs model tests](/lore/recovery-needs-model-tests): Test sequences of failures and recoveries against explicit invariants.
- [Golden signals expose overload](/lore/golden-signals-expose-overload): Measure latency, traffic, errors, and saturation, including failed work.
- [Shared schemas need a transition period](/lore/schema-changes-need-a-transition): Keep old and new representations usable while consumers migrate.
- [Durable timers need recovery](/lore/durable-timers-need-recovery): Persist scheduled intent when losing a worker must not lose its deadlines.
- [Request lifetime is not durability](/lore/request-lifetime-is-not-durability): Worker waitUntil has a shared post-response allowance; required work needs a durable marker and redrive.

